    "username": "emollick",
    "nickname": "Ethan Mollick",
    "text": "I was an early tester of GPT-5.6 Sol. I was asked to not share demos until after launch but it is a very good model.\n\nIt is of similar ability, but quite different feel, than Fable. Fable wants to go off and do work on its own pace, Sol is faster but works with you in steps more.",
    "quoted_tweet": null,
    "url": "https://twitter.com/emollick/status/2074712677755035907",
    "time": "2026-07-08 12:30",
    "created_at": "Wed Jul 08 04:30:23 +0000 2026",
    "id_str": "2074712677755035907",
    "is_retweet": false
  },
  {
    "username": "emollick",
    "nickname": "Ethan Mollick",
    "text": "I found myself switching between Fable and Sol depending on task. Sol for back-and-forth tasks, especially when I had not yet figured out what I needed exactly, Fable for very long tasks where I could define what I wanted, and Sol Pro for really hard problems.",
    "quoted_tweet": null,
